  "null": "each gene keeps the NUMBER of species it is present in and loses which ones. A null free to change prevalence would make two ubiquitous genes look like a discovery",
  "cannot_do": "species are not phylogenetically independent, so a null that draws them independently overstates how surprising a co-occurrence is: every excess here is a ceiling on the evidence, not the evidence. A species-tree-aware null is what would settle a pair, and this project does not hold one. Nothing here calls a pair a dependency",
